  <text xml:lang="la">
    <body>
      <div type="poem" n="3.4" xml:id="O-3.4-poem">
        <lg type="couplet">
          <pb n="51" facs="#O-3.4-p51" />
          <fw type="header" place="top">III, III, 14 — IIII, 37.</fw>
          <fw type="pageNum" place="top">51</fw>
          <label type="source-heading">IIII.</label>
          <l n="1" xml:id="O-3.4-l1" facs="#O-3.4-zone-1">Dure vir, inposito tenerae custode puellae</l>
          <l n="2" xml:id="O-3.4-l2" facs="#O-3.4-zone-2" rend="indent">Nil agis: ingeniost quaeque tuenda suo.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="3" xml:id="O-3.4-l3" facs="#O-3.4-zone-3">Siqua metu dempto castast, ea denique castast;</l>
          <l n="4" xml:id="O-3.4-l4" facs="#O-3.4-zone-4" rend="indent">Quae, quia non liceat, non facit, illa facit.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="5" xml:id="O-3.4-l5" facs="#O-3.4-zone-5">Ut iam servaris bene corpus, adultera mens est:</l>
          <l n="6" xml:id="O-3.4-l6" facs="#O-3.4-zone-6" rend="indent">Nec custodiri, ne velit, illa potest,</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="7" xml:id="O-3.4-l7" facs="#O-3.4-zone-7">Nec corpus servare potes, licet omnia claudas;</l>
          <l n="8" xml:id="O-3.4-l8" facs="#O-3.4-zone-8" rend="indent">Omnibus exclusis intus adulter erit.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="9" xml:id="O-3.4-l9" facs="#O-3.4-zone-9">Cui peccare licet, peccat minus: ipsa potestas</l>
          <l n="10" xml:id="O-3.4-l10" facs="#O-3.4-zone-10" rend="indent">Semina nequitiae languidiora facit.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="11" xml:id="O-3.4-l11" facs="#O-3.4-zone-11">Desine, crede mihi, vitia inritare vetando:</l>
          <l n="12" xml:id="O-3.4-l12" facs="#O-3.4-zone-12" rend="indent">Obsequio vinces aptius illa tuo.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="13" xml:id="O-3.4-l13" facs="#O-3.4-zone-13">Vidi ego nuper equum contra sua vincla tenacem</l>
          <l n="14" xml:id="O-3.4-l14" facs="#O-3.4-zone-14" rend="indent">Ore reluctanti fulminis ire modo;</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="15" xml:id="O-3.4-l15" facs="#O-3.4-zone-15">Constitit, ut primum concessas sensit habenas</l>
          <l n="16" xml:id="O-3.4-l16" facs="#O-3.4-zone-16" rend="indent">Frenaque in effusa laxa iacere iuba.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="17" xml:id="O-3.4-l17" facs="#O-3.4-zone-17">Nitimur in vetitum semper cupimusque negata:</l>
          <l n="18" xml:id="O-3.4-l18" facs="#O-3.4-zone-18" rend="indent">Sic interdictis inminet aeger aquis.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="19" xml:id="O-3.4-l19" facs="#O-3.4-zone-19">Centum fronte oculos, centum cervice gerebat</l>
          <l n="20" xml:id="O-3.4-l20" facs="#O-3.4-zone-20" rend="indent">Argus: et hos unus saepe fefellit Amor;</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="21" xml:id="O-3.4-l21" facs="#O-3.4-zone-21">In thalamum Danae ferro saxoque perennem</l>
          <l n="22" xml:id="O-3.4-l22" facs="#O-3.4-zone-22" rend="indent">Quae fuerat virgo tradita, mater erat:</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="23" xml:id="O-3.4-l23" facs="#O-3.4-zone-23">Penelope mansit, quamvis custode carebat,</l>
          <l n="24" xml:id="O-3.4-l24" facs="#O-3.4-zone-24" rend="indent">Inter tot iuvenes intemerata procos.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="25" xml:id="O-3.4-l25" facs="#O-3.4-zone-25">Quidquid servatur, cupimus magis, ipsaque furem</l>
          <l n="26" xml:id="O-3.4-l26" facs="#O-3.4-zone-26" rend="indent">Cura vocat: pauci, quod sinit alter, amant.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="27" xml:id="O-3.4-l27" facs="#O-3.4-zone-27">Nec facie placet illa sua, sed amore mariti:</l>
          <l n="28" xml:id="O-3.4-l28" facs="#O-3.4-zone-28" rend="indent">Nescio quid, quod te ceperit, esse putant.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="29" xml:id="O-3.4-l29" facs="#O-3.4-zone-29">Non proba fit, quam vir servat, sed adultera cara:</l>
          <l n="30" xml:id="O-3.4-l30" facs="#O-3.4-zone-30" rend="indent">Ipse timor pretium corpore maius habet.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="31" xml:id="O-3.4-l31" facs="#O-3.4-zone-31">Indignere licet, iuvat inconcessa voluptas:</l>
          <l n="32" xml:id="O-3.4-l32" facs="#O-3.4-zone-32" rend="indent">Sola placet, ‘timeo’ dicere siqua potest.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="33" xml:id="O-3.4-l33" facs="#O-3.4-zone-33">Nec tamen ingenuam ius est servare puellam:</l>
          <l n="34" xml:id="O-3.4-l34" facs="#O-3.4-zone-34" rend="indent">Hic metus externae corpora gentis agat!</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="35" xml:id="O-3.4-l35" facs="#O-3.4-zone-35">Scilicet ut possit custos ‘ego’ dicere ‘feci’,</l>
          <l n="36" xml:id="O-3.4-l36" facs="#O-3.4-zone-36" rend="indent">In laudem servi casta sit illa tui?</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="37" xml:id="O-3.4-l37" facs="#O-3.4-zone-37">Rusticus est nimium, quem laedit adultera coniunx,</l>
          <fw type="signature" place="bottom">4*</fw>
          <pb n="52" facs="#O-3.4-p52" />
          <fw type="header" place="top">AMORUM</fw>
          <fw type="pageNum" place="top">52</fw>
          <l n="38" xml:id="O-3.4-l38" facs="#O-3.4-zone-38" rend="indent">Et notos mores non satis Urbis habet,</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="39" xml:id="O-3.4-l39" facs="#O-3.4-zone-39">In qua Martigenae non sunt sine crimine nati</l>
          <l n="40" xml:id="O-3.4-l40" facs="#O-3.4-zone-40" rend="indent">Romulus Iliades Iliadesque Remus.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="41" xml:id="O-3.4-l41" facs="#O-3.4-zone-41">Quo tibi formosam, si non nisi casta placebat?</l>
          <l n="42" xml:id="O-3.4-l42" facs="#O-3.4-zone-42" rend="indent">Non possunt ullis ista coire modis!</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="43" xml:id="O-3.4-l43" facs="#O-3.4-zone-43">Si sapis, indulge dominae vultusque severos</l>
          <l n="44" xml:id="O-3.4-l44" facs="#O-3.4-zone-44" rend="indent">Exue nec rigidi iura tuere viri</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="45" xml:id="O-3.4-l45" facs="#O-3.4-zone-45">Et cole, quos dederit (multos dabit) uxor, amicos:</l>
          <l n="46" xml:id="O-3.4-l46" facs="#O-3.4-zone-46" rend="indent">Gratia sic minimo magna labore venit;</l>
        </lg>
        <lg type="couplet">
          <l n="47" xml:id="O-3.4-l47" facs="#O-3.4-zone-47">Sic poteris iuvenum convivia semper inire</l>
          <l n="48" xml:id="O-3.4-l48" facs="#O-3.4-zone-48" rend="indent">Et, quae non dederis, multa videre domi.</l>
        </lg>
      </div>
    </body>
    <back>
      <div type="editorial-notes">
        <head>Transcription notes</head>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-1" n="1" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l1">The printed poem heading is IIII., using four strokes. It is encoded separately from the opening verse. The source spelling inposito is retained.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-2" n="2" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l2">The source prints the contraction ingeniost as one word; it is not silently expanded in the transcription.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-3" n="3" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l3">Both occurrences of castast are printed contractions and retained as written.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-6" n="6" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l6">The source ends this verse with a comma. The punctuation has not been regularized to match the following semicolon.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-11" n="11" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l11">The printed spelling inritare is retained, as is inminet at18.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-32" n="32" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l32">The source places quotation marks around timeo only. Their placement is retained with schematic curly quotes.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-35" n="35" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l35">Ego and feci are separately quoted in the print, with dicere between them. The question continues through the following verse.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-37" n="37" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l37">The printed signature 4* follows this verse at the foot of page51. It is encoded as forme work; the couplet continues on page52.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-38" n="38" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l38">The source capitalizes Urbis here and Martigenae in the next verse.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-40" n="40" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l40">The source prints Iliades Iliadesque; the repeated name is retained without editorial correction.</note>
        <note xml:id="O-3.4-note-45" n="45" type="observation" target="#O-3.4-l45">The parenthetical multos dabit is printed inside the verse and retained along with its surrounding commas and final colon.</note>
      </div>
    </back>
